The '''People's Assembly of Bolodun and Kuvari Islands''' is the unicameral national legislature of the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]]. It consists of 100 members elected from the country's fourteen member districts and sits in [[Ominira]]. The Assembly was established in 1927 under the new constitution adopted after independence in 1926, replacing the transitional legislative arrangements that had grown out of the [[Kuvari War]].

== Role ==

The People's Assembly is the legislative branch of the state. It writes and passes laws, approves the budget, and exercises oversight of the [[Yohannes Bari|president]] and the government. As a unicameral body, it combines the legislative and representative functions in a single chamber.

== Electoral districts ==

Members are elected from electoral districts apportioned by population. Each [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands#Geography|island]] is divided into enough districts to match its share of the national population, so that each member represents roughly the same number of residents — approximately one member per 1,155 people under the 2025 census counts. Every inhabited island is guaranteed at least one seat regardless of population, so that even the smallest islands retain representation in the Assembly. The largest islands return several members, while the smallest islands return a single member each.

