== Elections ==

Members of the People's Assembly serve two-year terms. Elections are held on a fixed national date, 11 November, in every even-numbered year. The most recent election was held on 11 November 2024; the next election is scheduled for 11 November 2026.

== History ==

The Assembly was formed in 1927, the year after independence, under the [[Constitution of the Bolodun and Kuvari Islands (1927)|constitution of 1927]]. The new constitution replaced the earlier two-administration arrangement — the Sudanese Kaftian administration on [[Bolodun]] and the Kuvari administration on [[Tumala]] — with a single national chamber and fourteen districts, one for each major island, sending representatives to the Assembly.

